        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Premenstrual symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For 7–10 days before menses: irritability, tearfulness, feeling unable to cope at school, breast tenderness, bloating, and more migraines. Symptoms improve by day 1–2 of bleeding. Cycles regular at 28–30 days; mood is okay between cycles. No suicidal ideation."
      }
